title: After Frankfurt
subtitle: The revolutionary year is over.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: congress_number = 10 and first_year_done = 0 and rf_over = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
var RF = window.RF;
Q.first_year_done = 1;
Q.first_year_verdict = RF.verdict(Q, 3);
Q.first_year_mark = Q.first_year_verdict ? 1 : 0;
Q.first_year_grade = Q.unity >= 70 && Q.autonomy >= 50 && Q.splits == 0 ? 2 :
    (Q.unity >= 50 ? 1 : 0);
!}

#The interim verdict from the lean design: a player who stops after the
#first year still gets a closing page. It reads the record (RF.verdict)
#and the party's unity, autonomy and splits.

= After Frankfurt

[? if first_year_grade = 2 : The party has come through defeat with its unity and its own mind. ?][? if first_year_grade = 1 : The party has survived the year, weaker and angrier than it entered it. ?][? if first_year_grade = 0 : The party has come out of the year divided, and less its own master than before. ?] It is led by the <span class="f-[+ leader +]">[+ leader_name +]</span>.

[? if first_year_mark = 1 : What the year will be remembered for: ?]

[+ first_year_verdict +]

The inflation is over. American money is coming, and with it a stabilisation that will test a party built for a revolutionary crisis. You can end the game here, or lead the party on.

- @go_on: Lead the party on.
- @end_here: End the game here.

@go_on
title: Lead the party on.

The party goes into the election campaign.

@end_here
title: End the game here.
game-over: true

The game ends here, with the party at the threshold of the stabilisation years.
